WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.326 --> 00:00:03.690
(soft instrumental music)

00:00:03.690 --> 00:00:05.480
- I'm reporting from Taiwan

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:08.530
where this island is increasingly
becoming a focal point

00:00:08.530 --> 00:00:11.000
between US and China tensions.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.830
I'm going to take you to three places

00:00:12.830 --> 00:00:16.380
to explain how the competitions
between the two superpowers

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:18.610
from the tech to the military

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:21.053
could determine the future of this place.

00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.630
But first, a little
history about why Taiwan

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:27.123
is so important to China.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:31.410
This island was where the
Chinese Nationalist Party fled

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:33.500
after its military defeat at the end

00:00:33.500 --> 00:00:36.069
of the Chinese Civil War in 1949.

00:00:36.069 --> 00:00:39.902
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.770
Today, Taiwan holds democratic elections,

00:00:47.770 --> 00:00:52.060
uses a different passport,
and has its own distinct flag.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.460
And while some politicians here

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.040
support closer ties with Beijing,

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.083
many people have grown
uncomfortable with that idea.

00:01:00.290 --> 00:01:04.860
This, our first stop, the
capital of Taiwan, Taipei.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.460
Here growing numbers of young Taiwanese

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:09.700
supports closer ties with the US

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:12.372
over closer relations with China.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:15.872
(warm instrumental music)

00:01:25.344 --> 00:01:29.761
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:01:32.090 --> 00:01:34.140
- Security experts say
this kind of statement

00:01:34.140 --> 00:01:37.333
could mean military actions
that puts the US into conflict.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:41.380
And recently there has been
a lot more military activity

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:44.283
in the strait between the
island and Mainland China.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.037
- This is the Strait of Taiwan.

00:01:47.037 --> 00:01:48.500
"The Wall Street Journal" will tell you

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:51.020
of how many Chinese
warplanes were in the region

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.610
using information from
Taiwan's Defense Ministry

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.810
and would find that in 2020,

00:01:55.810 --> 00:01:58.900
China sent about 380
warplanes to this region.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:03.272
But this year there were
already about 290 warplanes.

00:02:03.272 --> 00:02:07.105
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:02:09.594 --> 00:02:12.170
US officials and former
Taiwanese military leaders

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:14.000
say Taiwan will need to do more

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.311
to be able to fend off
an invasion from China,

00:02:17.311 --> 00:02:20.460
especially since China has about 100 times

00:02:20.460 --> 00:02:23.163
as many ground force personnel as Taiwan.

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:27.700
China's annual military budget
is also 25 times larger.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:29.450
So in an attempt to fill the gap,

00:02:29.450 --> 00:02:32.817
last year Taiwan increased
the military spending by 10%

00:02:32.817 --> 00:02:35.723
and has been purchasing
weapons from the US.

00:02:36.800 --> 00:02:38.350
But some military analysts say

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.530
it's not in China's interest to attack.

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.340
The seas are rough, and Taiwan's coastline

00:02:43.340 --> 00:02:45.770
make it difficult for a warship to land.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:48.670
Most importantly, an invasion could prompt

00:02:48.670 --> 00:02:52.113
a military response from the
US which would likely escalate.

00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:55.320
But if not a military conflict,

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:58.300
Taiwan provides at least
one more area of competition

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.510
between the US and China.

00:03:00.510 --> 00:03:03.969
Behind me is the headquarters of TSMC,

00:03:03.969 --> 00:03:07.080
the world's largest contract chip maker.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:10.350
Its chips ends up in our
smartphone and laptop,

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:13.760
but now because of a global chip shortage,

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:17.800
Taiwan is becoming more
important to the US and China.

00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:21.310
That's because TSMC controls
more than 90% of the market

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:24.245
for the most advanced semiconductors.

00:03:24.245 --> 00:03:28.078
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:03:34.101 --> 00:03:38.223
TSMC has tried to walk the
line between China and the US,

00:03:38.223 --> 00:03:40.330
but the tension between
these two countries

00:03:40.330 --> 00:03:44.480
has made this difficult,
especially after Washington

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:49.360
restrict Chinese telecom
giants Huawei's access to TSMC

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:51.453
over national security concerns.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:55.600
The Trump administration has
instructed American supplier

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.700
to stop working with TSMC

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.379
if it kept exporting chips to Huawei.

00:04:00.379 --> 00:04:04.212
(dramatic instrumental music)

00:04:13.650 --> 00:04:15.760
To reduce its dependence on Taiwan,

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.500
China has made chip
manufacturing a priority.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.566
So has the US with a
commitment of $15 billion

00:04:21.566 --> 00:04:24.100
to building up that sector.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:25.820
- We're investing aggressively in areas

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.560
like semiconductors and batteries.

00:04:27.560 --> 00:04:31.680
That's what they're doing
in others, so must we.

00:04:31.680 --> 00:04:32.818
- [Joyu] But it will take years

00:04:32.818 --> 00:04:36.250
before these efforts bear
fruit, giving the US and China

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.673
yet another reason to focus on Taiwan.

00:04:41.413 --> 00:04:43.017
- [Christopher] Thank you.

00:04:43.017 --> 00:04:44.510
- [Tsai] I suppose we should do this.

00:04:44.510 --> 00:04:46.067
- [Christopher] We can do that, okay.

00:04:46.067 --> 00:04:50.360
(woman speaking in foreign language)

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:51.920
And I can say with confidence

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.140
that the United States'
partnership with Taiwan

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:57.160
is stronger than ever.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:59.660
- Ultimately, the future of this island

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:03.050
is going to be a key challenge
for the Biden administration.

00:05:03.050 --> 00:05:05.690
So the US will have to
find the right balance

00:05:05.690 --> 00:05:08.210
between supporting
Taiwan while making sure

00:05:08.210 --> 00:05:11.816
ongoing tensions with China
doesn't escalate further.

00:05:11.816 --> 00:05:15.649
(dramatic instrumental music)

